  "tagline": "Claude works on your local files and apps, on a schedule.",
  "description": "Cowork is Anthropic's agent for knowledge work and, according to Anthropic, uses the same agentic architecture as Claude Code; Anthropic does not name the Claude Agent SDK, so the harness pick is inferred from that statement and from a TechCrunch report that Cowork is built on the SDK. Since October 6, 2026, new sessions on Pro and Max plans run in the cloud: the agent loop and code execution run in a per-session sandbox on Anthropic's servers, and the Claude Desktop app relays access to connected local folders, the browser and the computer. By default Claude browses in a pane built into Claude Desktop; people who already use Claude in Chrome keep working in their own browser. Local sessions, kept for earlier tasks and existing desktop deployments, run code in a Linux VM on the device. Cowork shares account memory with chat in the cloud, runs scheduled tasks remotely, coordinates sub-agents and Dispatch tasks, and is extended with MCP connectors, skills, plugins and hooks; organisations can export its activity over OpenTelemetry. Anthropic's support center documents this architecture, and a more detailed security architecture overview is available on request from its Trust Center.",
